999:📋 **LADDER (lane-a) — `f2289-1-recorder-assayer-hash-divergence` AUTHORED + QUEUED s2290 (FIRE-AUTHORED, attended review welcome).** Executes F-2289-1, which s2289 priced as *"the best-priced real defect on the board and fire-authorable as a DIAGNOSTIC, not a cure."* 🔑 **The premise was VERIFIED against main at authoring time rather than inherited, and it narrows the task from a search into a diff: BOTH endpoints call the SAME function on the SAME input** — `agentOrdersEventLogHash(snapshotStandingOrders())` at `scripts/gr-sim.mjs:260` (writer) and `scripts/assay-replay-agent.mjs:174` (reader), the function being `src/game/RunTape.ts:271`, which hashes **only** `orders_replaced` entries with `at`/`seq` stripped. **So this is NOT two hash implementations disagreeing — one function on one input shape producing two results means `snapshotStandingOrders()` is returning different content in the two contexts, and the task is to dump both sequences and diff them.** Four hypotheses ride with it, each a lead from reading the code and **none a conclusion**, with refutation valued equally to confirmation: **H1 cross-attempt accumulation** — `installedExecutor` is module-level and neither call site calls `resetStandingOrders()`, which `scripts/gr-sim-campaign.mjs:91` *does* call, and the divergence is conditional exactly where a 10-attempt campaign differs from a 1-launch run (Night Shift claims `889d9357` and replays `889d9357`; Hill Mine, attempt 10 of 10, does not); **H2** rejected orders counted on one side only (the recorder sees every attempt, the replay only what the tape retained); **H3** the terminal-instant boundary F-ASSAY-E2E-2 already documents at `scripts/gr-sim.mjs:250–259`; **H4** the empty-log fallback at `src/agent/StandingOrders.ts:477`, which returns a legitimate-looking hash when no executor is installed. ⛔ **The firewall forbids curing, and that is the design rather than caution:** this defect already carries one workaround shipped on top of it (F-2289-2 — the door discloses the replayed hash, so a rejection is converted into an acceptance by copying it in), and **the one signal the check exists to produce is precisely the signal that workaround destroys**. The master also forbids rewriting any retained tape, since a curated tape is how this got buried the first time. Scope 4 sweeps every retained tape for claim-vs-replay disagreement — **that table is what tells the owner whether F-2289-1 cost the county one standing or many.** GATE: none — lane-a is `ahead=0 tracked-dirt=0` USABLE, verified at queue time.
1042:🚨 **F-2276-1 — THE DOOR STRUCTURALLY REFUSES AN HONEST NIGHT SHIFT WIN, AND THE ANNOUNCE IS QUEUED BEHIND IT (s2276, drain of gauntlet-heat5 at `5ffb9bcb0`; OWNER DESK — DESIGN FORK, NOT FIRE-AUTHORABLE).** `e1-night-shift` secures only at **wave 25**, and the earliest such win is **22,501 ticks** — measured on FOUR independent attempts, all `secured=true waves=25 timeMs=750033` — against a standings ceiling of **18,000** (both accepted E1 reels land at exactly 18000). Its POST is refused `{"ok":false,"error":"bad_payload"}`. ⚖️ **So the contract is unwinnable through the public door BY ANYONE — this is not a rider skill wall**, and it is **distinct from the known 18,001 off-by-one** (F-ASSAY-E2E-2, `specs/agent-play/tape-contract.md:26`) that silent default banking cures for Twin Banks: Night Shift misses by **4,501 ticks** and nothing a rider does can close it. ✗ **The enforcement site is NOT in this repo** — targeted greps of `functions/`, `src/`, `scripts/` for `18000` return only an unrelated timer at `scripts/backfill-agent-tapes.mjs:40`; the cap lives server-side in the deployed standings endpoint, which a fire cannot read. ➡️ **Three cures and all three are design forks** (raise the ceiling · make it per-contract · change Night Shift's secure condition), so the owner rules. **RECOMMENDATION: per-contract or raised ceiling BEFORE the announce** — it is the smallest cure and invalidates no existing standing. The live LAUNCH FOCUS row records the owner's own order to *"secure and publish + announce the first version now"*; announcing a six-contract county with one contract unwinnable at the door is the kind of thing the announcement should not be first to discover. Evidence: `reviews/gauntlet-heat5-best-effort.md`, `artifacts/gauntlet-heat5-20260824/e1-night-shift/`.
