1110:🟡 **F-2239-1 (s2239 2026-08-23, AIM REFUTED BY MEASUREMENT, BANKED WITH ITS MECHANISM — TWO GUARDS IN ONE BATTERY APPLY OPPOSITE ID-SCOPE RULES AND THE DIVERGENCE IS LOAD-BEARING).** The dry-board aim was `findings-state-guard.mjs`'s `scan` (`:103`): it assigns a row's state to **every** F-ID in the 90-char subject zone (subject-ALL), while `desk-state-audit.mjs` — chained in the SAME `test:ledger-guards` battery — deliberately applies **subject-FIRST**, its clause stating that "an id merely CITED inside another finding's subject carries no state". Two rules for one question, one of them documented and verified, the other never examined. It reads exactly like [F-2219-1]'s shape (one arm cured, its sibling left bare) and like the class its predecessor named: *who else can write into the text you match on?* — here, a fire, later, in prose, truthfully. 📊 **MEASURED ON THE LIVE BOARD, detector validated against a purpose-built fixture FIRST (the F-2215-1 duty — my control asserts it can SEE a manufactured citation-inheritance conflict before I believe it about the board): `tasks/BACKLOG.md` carries 740 rows with a state, 53 with >1 F-ID in the subject zone, and 25 ids whose state arrives ONLY by citation. Conflicts under the shipped subject-ALL rule: **0**. Conflicts under subject-FIRST: **0**. The gate is `PASS` (551 subjects / 382 closed / 169 open / double-state 0).** ⛔ **REFUTED, AND ON A STRUCTURAL REASON RATHER THAN A COUNT: subject-ALL is not a defect, it is LOAD-BEARING.** 9 of the 25 are **compound closure rows** — `✅ F-2189-1 + F-2189-2 — SHIPPED`, `✅ F-ASSAY-E2E-9 + F-ASSAY-E2E-10 — SHIPPED`, `✅ F-1741-1..5 / F-1755-1 CLOSED s1856` — where subject-FIRST would **silently drop the second finding's closure**, converting a correctly-closed finding into an unstated one. The cure would have manufactured the debt it was meant to find. ⚖️ **AND MY OWN CLASSIFIER'S REMAINING 16 IS AN OVER-COUNT, REPORTED HONESTLY RATHER THAN AS A HEADLINE (the s2230 duty: price a