WER IS AS OFTEN "BOTH ARE RIGHT" AS "ONE IS BROKEN". Ask what each tool's verdict is FOR before assuming the divergence is drift.** ⭐ And the streak's own rule paid again: testing the inherited aim cost ~35 minutes and returned the rest of the fire, where shipping the "obvious" cure would have cost a fire AND corrupted 9 ledger rows.
1135:🟢 **F-2247-1 + F-2247-2 (s2247 2026-08-23, FOUND AND CURED THE SAME FIRE ON A DRY BOARD — THE INHERITED CORPUS-vs-CLAIM AXIS, TAKEN AND LIVE ON ITS FIRST SUBJECT. GATE: none — this row is a completion.)** 🧭 **THE INHERITED AIM WAS TESTED BEFORE IT WAS SPENT ON, AND IT PAID ON THE FIRST INSTRUMENT.** s2246 handed forward one question — *is the subject set as wide as the sentence the tool prints next?* — and explicitly retired the five-tool census that preceded it. Applied to the SIX gate legs reached by `npm run` alias (a population any "bare legs" census misses by construction), `citation-title-guard` is the MODEL and is banked SOUND: it prints *"This verdict covers `tasks/**` only"* IN the verdict and names the `2,123` citations in `219` tracked `.md` it does NOT gate, citing the owner scope ruling F-1252-1. **A tool that states its own scope in its verdict is what the cured ones below now do.** 🎯 **F-2247-1 — `ruling-propagation-guard`, chained bare in `test:ledger-guards`. Its verdict is defined by ROLE — *"no REFUSAL cites a finding the owner has already ruled"*, universal over refusals — while its subject test was SIX EXACT KEY SPELLINGS.** 📊 **MEASURED on the live tree: `17` of the `44` refusing leaves (**38.6%**) carry NONE of the six, so the scan joined an EMPTY string and was structurally incapable of redding on them whatever they said — **38,681 chars of refusal prose unread, 13 of the 17 citing an F-id.** The tree holds **138** reason/note spellings, and the guard was reading `closedReason` (4 uses or fewer) while ignoring `closureReason` (24), `drainNotes` (172), `note` (160) and `authorNotes` (146) — **the three commonest reason-bearing keys in the entire tree.**** 🔑 **THE PROVENANCE IS THE SHARPEST PART: this file's own comments say it MIRRORS `drain-block-check.mjs`, and it does — for the terminal-status set, and for the leaf definition, where the comment calls the fidelity *"load-bearing"*. It mirrored its sibling in two places out of three and stopped at the one that decides WHAT IT READS.** ⚖️ **SEVERITY STATED HONESTLY AND NOT INFLATED: LATENT. Every hit I read resolved to a citation, not a basis, so today's PASS was TRUE — verified, not assumed. What earns it a row is that the blindness lands in a GATE, in the permissive direction, in the DEFAULT mode the battery uses.** 🛠️ **CURE: widen to the spellings whose NAME states the refusal BASIS (+8, including session-stamped variants — `stoppedNote_s1263` and `stoppedNote` are one record, the anchoring mistake s1249 already paid for), and DECLARE the residue always, including the happy path (F-2208-1). Residue **17 → 5**, each named on stdout; the PASS sentence now reads *"no READABLE refusal…"* whenever anything went unread.** 🚦 **WHY NOT THE FULL WIDENING, AND THE BOUNDARY IS MEASURED RATHER THAN STYLISTIC — this is the half a weaker cure gets wrong: scanning the narrative fields (`note`, `drainNotes`, `authorNotes`) reds on THREE live leaves and **ALL THREE REDS ARE FALSE.** `b4v2-picnic-stake-pressure` and `vp-02e-jumper-8way-activation` each RECORD that a ruling was propagated (*"(F-2085-1 RULED)"*, *"OWNER RULING PROPAGATED s1655"*), and `lane-vp-02b-jumper-slot-red`'s drainNotes REFUTES the citation outright (*"It is NOT -- F-1166-1 … treats this spec as GREEN"*). **In a narrative field an F-id is as likely to be a refutation or a propagation record as a basis.** Redding there would turn this guard's OWN remedy text — *"say so without naming the ruled finding"* — into an instruction to DELETE propagation records, i.e. to corrupt correct bookkeeping under the Retention Law, and a guard that fires on ordinary correct work is excused into uselessness inside a week (F-1460-1). **So the 5 that remain DECLARE AND DO NOT RED** (F-2218-1's restraint). 🎯 **F-2247-2 — AND IT IS WHY "IMPORT THE SIBLING" WOULD HAVE SHIPPED THE SIBLING'S DEFECT.** `drain-block-check`'s resolver excludes retired reasons by naming ONE spelling, `priorBlockedReason`; the tree holds **SIX** (`priorStoppedReason`, `priorStopNote_s1206`, `priorStopNote_s1288`, `priorBlockReason_s1110_SUPERSEDED`, `priorBlockClass`). Worse, the survivors rank FIRST: `priorStoppedReason` matches its closure-stem test on *"stop"* while the live `closureReason` does NOT — **so a retired reason OUTRANKED the real one.** 📊 **MEASURED: `2` of the `42` terminal-closed leaves resolved to `priorStoppedReason` (`agent-rung-honest-gate`, `ap-06b-panel-ladder-and-voice`), and BOTH carry a `closureReason` stating the actual supersession. `agent-rung-honest-gate`'s own `authorNotes` warns IN WORDS — *"READ THIS BEFORE THE PRIOR REASON BELOW, WHICH THE RULING OVERTURNS"* — and the instrument picked exactly the overturned one.** That is precisely the harm the file's own comment describes for `priorBlockedReason` (*"printing that as the closure cause would be WORSE than silence"*), reached by a spelling the exclusion did not cover. **Exclude the CLASS, not the member.** ✅ **NEUTRAL BEFORE LANDING (F-1274-2), control asserting its own validity first (F-2215-1 — *"pre-cure arm produced 154 B, rc 0 — it really ran"*): `ruling-propagation-guard` is verdict- and rc-neutral (still PASS, rc 0) over a corpus **12 leaves wider**; `drain-block-check` is byte-identical in 4 of 5 modes, and the ONE divergence is the intended correction, rc unchanged.** 🔒 **`scripts/refusal-reason-corpus-guard.test.mjs` — 13 arms, 0.9 s, rooted in `test:ledger-guards`.** 🔬 **TEETH, every variant manufactured on a scratch copy whose edit ASSERTS ITS ANCHOR APPLIED: PRE-CURE both files reds **9 of 13** (7 from the guard, 2 from the sibling), and each over-general cure is caught by exactly the reverse control built for it — scan-the-narrative-fields reds the propagation-record control · declare-only-on-failure reds the happy-path arm **ALONE** · widen-but-leave-the-verdict-unqualified reds the scope arm **ALONE** · exclude-every-reason-ish-key reds the "must not swallow a legitimate closure reason" control.** ⚠️ **TWO OF MY OWN ARMS WERE LYING AND THE SWEEP CAUGHT BOTH — this is the method lesson and it cost the fire its most useful half-hour.** (1) The pre-cure arm reddened with the FILE PATH as the test name, not a test name: the pre-cure copy does not export the symbols the cure adds, so the suite died at MODULE LOAD and reddened **9 arms while testing nothing.** A missing export is a CONSTRUCTION failure, not evidence about the defect; the imports of added symbols are now LAZY, so a pre-cure copy still loads and the arms testify behaviourally. (2) The arm named *"declares on the HAPPY path"* asserted through the CLI — but `main()` is `import.meta.url`-anchored, so **no fixture can drive the live board to `unreadable === 0`**, and the arm passed identically against a declare-only-on-failure variant. **It was asserting the happy path from a board that has never been happy.** The decision is now extracted and exercised directly, WITH a separate arm on the call site (F-2209-1: extracting a decision to make it testable creates a new untested seam). 🔭 **REACHABILITY AUDIT DISCHARGED (s2226's duty) AND IT EARNED ITS KEEP FOR THE THIRD FIRE RUNNING: after seven variants, `2` of 13 arms had reddened NOWHERE — both reverse controls on the retired/authoring exclusions. The variant that reaches them is the one a next fire is most likely to WRITE: adopt the sibling's stem match wholesale WITHOUT carrying its exclusions. It reds 7 arms including both. All 13 now red somewhere.** 💡 **REUSABLE, and it sharpens the inherited axis rather than merely confirming it: s2246 said a subject test that admits by FORMAT under a claim defined by ROLE is the shape. **The correction is that WIDENING THE FORMAT IS NOT THE CURE — measured here, the full widening manufactures three false reds and turns the guard's remedy into an order to destroy evidence.** When the claim is a ROLE, ask which FIELDS PLAY THAT ROLE — a basis, a record, a refutation and an intent are four different things wearing one shape — then widen to the role and DECLARE the rest. And when a file says it MIRRORS a sibling, check WHICH PARTS: this one mirrored the status set and the leaf definition and not the corpus, and the sibling it would have imported was itself defective in the same direction.**
1159:🟢 **F-2228-1 (s2228 2026-08-23, FOUND AND CURED THE SAME FIRE ON A DRY BOARD — THE F-ID PREDICATE WAS IMPLEMENTED SEVEN TIMES IN THREE VARIANTS, AND BOTH POPULATIONS WERE WRONG IN OPPOSITE DIRECTIONS).** Executed s2227’s aim (A) — *which predicates are implemented MORE THAN ONCE, and do the copies still agree?* Censused live instruments (143 non-test, non-scratch scripts): **9 predicates implemented in ≥2 live files, 5 disagreeing.** The load-bearing one is `FINDING`. **The four LEDGER guards** (`findings-state-guard`, `blocker-panel-closed-guard`, `ruling-propagation-guard`, `stale-open-candidates`) read `/\bF-\d+-\d+\b/` and are **structurally BLIND to every lettered id** — F-DOOR-6, F-E2S-4, F-ASSAY-E2E-9, F-PT15-1 — measured **23 state-declaring subjects** in `BACKLOG.md` and **2 of the 33 live blocker-panel rows** invisible. A guard that cannot SEE a row can never red on it, so the miss is in the **PERMISSIVE** direction, in gate legs. **The three DESK guards** read `/F-(?:[A-Z0-9]{1,8}-)+\d+/` with **no trailing `\b`**, so they match INSIDE a longer token: `"F-1419-2s CURE"` yields `F-1419-2`. ⚠️ **SO F-2227-1’S RULE — “IMPORT THE SIBLING, DO NOT WRITE A FIFTH COPY” — WAS NECESSARY BUT NOT SUFFICIENT: THE SIBLING WAS ITSELF DEFECTIVE.** Adopting it verbatim manufactures a double-state conflict (✅ :1388 vs the citation at :1396) and **REDS `findings-state-guard` on a row that makes no state claim at all**. Measured, one variable, same ledger: **narrow 520 subjects / 0 conflicts · desk-verbatim 543 / 1 SPURIOUS · cure 543 / 0**. 🛠️ **CURE: one anchored pattern `/\bF-(?:[A-Z0-9]{1,8}-)+\d+\b/g` exported from `findings-state-guard.mjs`** (already the F-1261-1 home of the closure rule), imported by the other three. ✅ **BEHAVIOUR-NEUTRAL ON EVERY VERDICT, COVERAGE STRICTLY WIDER: `findings-state-guard` PASS (520→543 subjects, 0 conflicts) · `blocker-panel-closed-guard` PASS (30→32 of 33 panel rows now checked, census 461→492) · `ruling-propagation-guard` identi