eep the corpus for other stale cost/measurement citations"*); tonight supplies its second and third data points, and **both were found BY ACCIDENT while doing something else** — which is the strongest available argument that a deliberate sweep would find more. **GATE: none owed by the owner — this is a verification closing an evidence gap, plus two corrections to inherited figures.** A later fire may (a) re-measure this battery under deliberate load to settle the causal question in ⓘ(1), and (b) treat 227.3 s in one file / 56.2% of wall as a standing invitation to ask whether `gr-sim` should be split. Neither is urgent; neither should be built by reflex. Related: [F-2098-1], [F-2076-1], [F-1537-1], [F-2090-2], [F-1460-1], [F-1507-1], [F-1441-3], [F-1409-1], [F-1410-2].
