s one produces a false-ABSENT set, which gets BACKFILLED — so the owner receives duplicate news for merges already reported.** Publishing the same item twice is worse than doing nothing, and nothing in the pipeline would have said so. 🔧 **CURE (doc-only, `scripts/fire.md` GZ-01): the clause now points at the INSTRUMENT instead of teaching a manual grep** — `node scripts/gazette-backfill-sweep.mjs` has existed since s1608, **indexes citations verbatim and tests by PREFIX**, and is therefore immune to this defect at any abbreviation width on either side. **The prose describing a hand-rolled grep is rationale, not instructions**; that distinction is the whole fix. ✅ **BOARD STATE CONFIRMED TWICE BY INDEPENDENT METHODS: my hand 8-char truncation over 63 merges → 0 owed, and the instrument over its own wider 67-merge set → `reported 63 / dismissed 4 / candidates 0`, exit 0.** ⓘ **No new mechanism proposed, deliberately** — the correct instrument already exists and this clause already bars mechanising the sweep as a red guard (player-visibility is a judgement, F-1460-1s `cross-engine` fate). The defect was in what fires were told to do, not in what the factory can do. **GATE: none owed — closed on landing. The row closes the carried duty too: GZ-01 needs no sweep, and a fire that carries it forward again should RE-MEASURE first rather than inherit the claim.** Related: [F-1600-1], [F-1608-1], [F-1610-1], [F-1546-1].
