he sweep cannot see restores them as candidates **forever**, which is precisely the disease F-1600-1 named — *"a check that reports a discharged duty as owed reports it forever, and every fire pays the judgement cost again"* — and that cost is real: judging these six took the larger part of this fire's non-authoring budget. **Between a silent retirement and a permanent re-judgement tax, the retirement is the better failure, and it is at least written down.** ⓘ **WHAT WOULD ACTUALLY FIX IT, if a later fire wants it, is a purpose marker rather than a new file:** have the sweep count a hash as *dismissed* only when it appears on a line matching a declared marker (e.g. `NOT PLAYER-VISIBLE`), and report **two** numbers — reported *N*, dismissed *M*, candidates *K* — so the dismissals stay visible and re-judgeable instead of vanishing into the cited total. That is a ~10-line change to one script and it keeps every dismissal in the same file as the news it sits beside. **DO NOT build it as a red guard** — the same law bars that, and a WARN-level split is the whole ask. 📊 **Population, so the next fire knows the size of what is now invisible:** across the sweep's window (since 2026-08-05) **70 of 70** player-path-touching first-parent merges now read as cited; **four** of those are dismissals written this fire, and they are `6c780b621` (art run, premise spent and failed, artifacts + ledger only), `fc284845d` (desk walkthrough, ledger only), `f33380c92` (python verifier fix + scratch probes), `1a2871fd3` (delimiter re-encoding restoring grep over `Game.ts`). **GATE: none owed — this row is a pointer, not a debt.** A fire that wants the two-number split may build it under the WARN-level constraint above; a fire that does not need only know that a clean sweep is now a weaker signal than it looks. Related: [F-1600-1], [F-1546-1], [F-1599-1]. ✅ **CLOSED s1613 — the invited build LANDED: `f1612-1` merged `5624e6a7ff9633a61ac49c299da116f61f5759f0`.** This row's gate said *"none owed — this row is a pointer, not a debt. A fire that wants the two-number split may build it"*, so it could have sat open indefinitely without anyone being at fault; s1612 authored the master from it and s1613 gated and merged it **three fires after the finding was written**. 📐 **What shipped is the cure this row specified, with one thing it did not ask for:** the sweep now reports **three** numbers (`reported 67 / dismissed 4 / candidates 0` on 71 player-path merges) and prints the dismissed list, so the dismissals stay **re-judgeable** instead of vanishing into a cited total — the row's stated point. It stays **WARN-level, exit 0 in every state**, per the F-1600-1 constraint this row itself imposed. 🔑 **The one addition is the DEFAULT, and it is what keeps the cure from becoming its own disease:** present-but-unmarked classifies **reported**, never **candidate** — proved by a marker-removal control run drain-side in both directions (`71/0/0` ↔ `67/4/0`), the four falling back to REPORTED. Had it defaulted the other way, four discharged judgements would have re-entered the candidate queue forever. ⚠️ **Read alongside [F-1613-1], filed by the same drain: the retro-mark that produces `dismissed 4` depends on a blank line that severs a sentence, and the obvious repair reads `62/9` — sweeping `88530e3ef`, a merge this pipeline PUBLISHED AS NEWS, into dismissed.** Related: [F-1600-1], [F-1546-1], [F-1599-1], [F-1613-1].
