ead-automation`, `blockClass: owner-fork`, no master authored (correctly — HARD LIMIT, never invent scope). **Backfilled per F-1534-2 (s1534); cure + teeth at F-1535-1.** **GATE: closes when the owner answers (1)–(4); until then no BT-04 master may be authored.** ⚖️ **RULED 2026-08-09 — THE BLOCK IS LIFTED; SUPERSEDED s1614 (F-1614-1).** `OWNER RULINGS ROUNDUP #2`: *"blocked trio ALL GREENLIT (… bt-04 → planned)"*; the leaf is `status: planned` with `blockClass` removed since `fc284845d`. ⚠️ **BUT A GREENLIT PROGRAM IS NOT AN ANSWER TO FORKS (1)–(4), AND THIS ROW MUST NOT BE READ AS ONE.** The roundup records a decision to PROCEED, not parameters: it names no X for *auto-repair under X%*, no definition of *idle*, no ruling on the building-tiers Law 4 balance question, and nothing on the `autoPan` name collision with the shipped E2 pressure-arsenal mechanic. ➡️ **So §2E's HARD LIMIT still bites for anything touching them — a fire may not invent X or idle.** **GATE (RESTATED): the BLOCK is closed; what remains is PARAMETERS. Any BT-04 slice must either avoid forks (1)–(4) entirely or carry the owner's values for the ones it touches. RECOMMENDED NEXT ACT (attended, not fire): put the four forks to Robin as four concrete questions with recommendations — the program is already greenlit, so only the numbers are missing.**
