he sibling candidate `run3d-17-megaproject-site-stages` is NOT fire-authorable**: `assets/pilots/stamp-mill-3d/` already ships 11 stamp-mill GLBs for the TOWN pilot (`src/town/TownTavernPilot.ts:18`), and which of them the run-scene stages derive from is a consistency-law question **no spec line answers** — a design fork, so it goes to an attended session, not a fire. 💡 The class: an authorisation and a base are two different gates, and a ladder line can only ever grant the first. The thing that made this unauthorable was not on the ladder — it was in another lane's run log.
2691:🟢 **F-1395-1 (s1395, MEASURED — THE CENSUS DOC EXISTS; THE LADDER'S REAL GATE IS POST-LAUNCH).** F-1394-2 declared all four lanes PIPELINE-DRY because the F-CEN ladder's `READ-FIRST = the census doc` was "not in the repo", and put a cheap-and-unblocking ask on the owner's desk. **Both halves are wrong, and the second is the expensive one.** 📄 **(1) THE DOCUMENT IS TRACKED AND ALWAYS WAS:** `docs/bench/agent-playability-census.md` — 26 lines, 5,322 bytes, committed **`1078564b`** *"census: the agent-playability census — 41 contracts compiled (1 ready, 40 data-gap, 0 broken) + action ladder"*, last touched `07854e6b`; never deleted, never renamed (`--diff-filter=D` and `-R` over 200 commits surface only unrelated *map-census* queue retirements). **I did not take the finder's word for it — I read the file and mapped all eight rungs to their source lines:** F-CEN-1←`:16` (*"5 of 8 cannot boot even in a browser (empty harvestAnchors → silent decline to The Claim, contradicting live dispatch rows)"*) · F-CEN-2←`:14` (*"DustFlatsTile is complete dead code"*) · F-CEN-3←`:14` (fairground) · F-CEN-4←`:24`+`:16`+`:17` · F-CEN-5←`:23` · F-CEN-6←`:15` (*"picnic declares 3 loss stakes but every consumer .find()s the first"*) · F-CEN-7←`:15`+`:17` · F-CEN-8←`:13`. Its §THE ACTION LADDER is literally the thing "census action-ladder order" names. 🔍 **WHY THREE HONEST PROBES ALL MISSED A TRACKED FILE — and it is not carelessness, it is a repeatable search bug.** Two of them searched for the **citation's paraphrase instead of the cited text**: the masters say *"§E1-E2 gaps"* and *"silent drift risk"*, while the doc says `| E1-E2 |` as a **table cell** and *"drift risk"* — so `git grep` could only ever return the citing masters, which is exactly what s1394 observed and read as confirmation. The third probe, `find -iname "*census*"`, **DID return this file**; it was counted among "six unrelated hits". ⚠️ **A `find` hit whose filename contains the very word you are searching for deserves a `head` before it is called unrelated** — the doc names itself by its SUBJECT (agent-playability), every citation names it by its SECTION, and nothing on either surface says so. ⛔ **(2) THE RUNG CARRIES TWO CONJUNCTS AND ONLY ONE WAS EVER CHECKED. The ladder is `LADDERED **post-launch**` (this row's own line, and `BACKLOG:2515` — *"Marquee findings for post-launch ladders"*), and post-launch is UNSATISFIED:** `git tag` carries **zero version tags** (46 refs = 45 `archive-del/*` + `pre-m1` — the exact denominator trap F-1373-1 recorded), and `rf-05-fixed-version` is still `planned` with *"remaining = owner vE1.0 tag + final E1 walk blessing"*. ✅ **So the board IS dry and s1394's verdict was right — but for a reason it never tested, and the reason it did give would have cost an owner action for nothing:** filing a document that is already tracked, or re-scoping eight rungs whose source was never missing, and **at the end of it the ladder would still be parked**, because the gate that actually holds it is launch. 💡 **The class, and it is the sharper twin of "count the conjuncts": when a gate has two conditions and you find one apparently broken, the found one absorbs all the attention — the search STOPS at the first plausible blocker, and a wrong first answer prevents the second question from ever being asked.** The cure is cheap and mechanical: **enumerate every conjunct before diagnosing any of them.** ⓘ At my own expense: my own first goal-tree walker double-counted the root and invented a statusless leaf, which I nearly filed as a schema finding — the careful walker says **536 leaves, 18 non-terminal** (6 blocked · 7 planned · 3 building · 2 stopped), and **all 18 re-read at source this fire are legitimately gated**, a sixth independent road to the same dry verdict. ➡️ **ACTIONS: F-1394-2's owner ask WITHDRAWN (nothing to file). DO NOT author F-CEN-1..8 until launch closes.** When it does, all eight are genuinely fire-authorable with the census as READ-FIRST — F-CEN-2 (DustFlatsTile: `createDustFlatsTile` at `src/world/DustFlatsTile.ts:170` has zero callers outside its own file) and F-CEN-6 (picnic) are the most self-contained; **F-CEN-5 is materially thinner than the rest** (no file:line anchors in the census, and its governing `specs/agent-play/README.md` is DRAFT · REHEARSAL-GATED behind the open AP-03 ask).
2693:⛔ **F-1394-2 SUPERSEDED s1395 BY F-1395-1 — ITS CENTRAL FACTUAL CLAIM IS FALSE AND ITS OWNER ASK IS WITHDRAWN. The census doc EXISTS at `docs/bench/agent-playability-census.md` (tracked, committed `1078564b`, never deleted or renamed); s1394's own first probe HIT it and misclassified it as unrelated. Do NOT act on the ask below. The ladder is genuinely parked, but on the POST-LAUNCH gate — see F-1395-1. ORIGINAL ROW PRESERVED VERBATIM BELOW.** 🔺 **F-1394-2 (s1394, PIPELINE — THE CENSUS LADDER IS LABELLED "FIRE-AUTHORABLE" BUT ITS `READ-FIRST` SOURCE IS NOT IN THE REPO, SO NO FIRE CAN AUTHOR A RUNG OF IT).** With **all six queues empty and every goal leaf either merged, owner-gated, or STOPPED-do-not-requeue**, the board's only remaining authorable work is the census action-ladder — **F-CEN-1** (E7/E8 bootability, 5 empty-anchor contracts vs live dispatches) through **F-CEN-8** (escort-mode-as-data) — which this ledger marks *"fire-authorable in census action-ladder order, **READ-FIRST = the census doc**"*. **That document does not exist on disk.** Measured, not assumed, with three independent unchained probes: `find -iname "*census*"` returns six files, none of them it (map-census, glb-census, landmark-brightness, glow-mesa-retire, triage-2026-07-21, f1330-1); `git grep "E1-E2 gaps"` hits **only `tasks/lane-claim-geometry-declared.md` and `tasks/lane-dead-fields-sweep.md`** — the masters that *cite* the census; `git grep "silent drift risk"` hits **only the second of those**. The shipped census masters quote it by section (*"READ-FIRST: census §E1-E2 gaps 3-4 + §E3-E4 (damChannel)"*) and reproduce its verdicts as quoted fragments, which is why the five **already-queued** masters could be executed — **an attended session held the census in context and transcribed each rung as it queued it.** The eight LADDERED rungs never got that transcription. ⚠️ **So §2E's HARD LIMIT binds: the next work has no spec slice on disk, therefore a fire must NOT author it** — authoring F-CEN-1 from its one-line BACKLOG summary would be inventing scope against a source I cannot read, on live E7/E8 contract wiring. **PIPELINE-DRY: all four lanes (needs the census doc filed, or the rungs re-scoped).** ➡️ **OWNER/ATTENDED ASK, cheap and unblocking: file the census document into `docs/` or `reviews/` (it is presumably still in the 2026-08-02 attended session's context), or re-scope F-CEN-1..8 as self-contained one-paragraph WHY blocks the way the five shipped masters were.** Either one turns 8 parked rungs back into fire-authorable work. 💡 **The class: "fire-authorable" is a claim about the READER's access, not about the work's difficulty.** A ladder is only as authorable as its cited source is reachable, and a citation to something that lives in a session's context reads exactly like a citation to a file — right up until a fire tries to follow it.
2740:🟢 **F-1372-1 (s1372, MEASURED — NEGATIVE RESULT: NO SPEC SLICE IS LOST, BECAUSE SLICE IDS ARE NOT THE LEDGER’S KEY EITHER — AND THE NEW PART IS THAT ABSENCE FROM THE LEDGER IS *BIDIRECTIONAL*, SO THIS ENTIRE CLASS OF SWEEP HAS A SIGN AMBIGUITY AT ITS CORE.)** 🧭 **THE PROBE.** s1370 §K(3) offered two surfaces as *hypotheses, not work*; s1371 took the first (`reviews/` F-ids) and deliberately left the second. This is the second and last: **`specs/**` slices whose playable checkpoints no goal leaf claims.** Per s1371 §K(3) I derived what enumerates the set before counting it, and per s1371 §H(3) **every absence-grep in this fire ran UNCHAINED (`;`, never `&&`)**. 📐 **THE DENOMINATOR HAD TO BE DERIVED, AND THE DOCUMENT-CLASS TRAP s1371 PREDICTED IS REAL.** `specs/` = **77 files / 41 directories** and is **not one class**: RATIFIED specs · DRAFTs · **SEED / “DISCUSSION STATUS, NOT BUILDABLE”** docs (`token-connection`, `loot-and-builds`, `contract-editor`) · a **SUPERSEDED** spec (`outlaw-intelligence`) · **content bundles** (`epoch-saga/e3..e10`) · **recipes** (`town-3d/RECIPE.md`) · **file-per-slice dirs** (`m0`/`m1`/`m2`/`visual-polish`, where the ID is the *filename*). Slice IDs are uppercase tokens declared as `- **RF-01 — …**` or `SLICE PC-01:`. Extracting from declaration-shaped lines only: **133 candidates**, of which I dropped **5 measured false positives** (`F-1`..`F-5` in `e10-static-mechanic-DRAFT.md` are **finding ids inside a spec** — verified by reading `:265-269`) and **17 BUILD-PLAN per-epoch work-class templates** (`ENG-1`/`CON-1`/`ART-1`/`CER-1` recur for every epoch E2–E10; they are a *plan* vocabulary, not one spec’s slices) ⇒ **111 slice IDs**. ⚖️ **THE STRUCTURAL RESULT, AND IT SETTLES THE PREMISE BEFORE THE RESIDUE MATTERS: 60 in `goals.json` · 95 in `BACKLOG` · 60 in BOTH · 0 in goals-only.** **`goals.json` is a STRICT SUBSET of BACKLOG.** So the question as posed — *“no goal leaf claims it”* — would have reported **51 misses**, and **35 of those are lawfully tracked BACKLOG rungs**. Asking the goal tree is asking the wrong index, exactly as F-ids were the wrong index in F-1371-1. ✅ **THE 16 IN NEITHER, ALL READ AT SOURCE, NOT SAMPLED — ALL 16 LAWFUL, IN FOUR DISTINCT WAYS.** **(1) `ST-00`..`ST-07` (8 — the largest block, and the one that looked like a real finding):** `specs/e10-static-mechanic-DRAFT.md` is headed **RATIFIED 2026-08-01** by the owner *(“(Q1) option (a) (Q2) option (a) (Q3) option (a)”)*, so 8 slices of an owner-ratified spec appear in no ledger. **Innocent, and already known:** the ruling’s scope clause is ***post-launch*** — recorded at `BACKLOG:2406` and `specs/e10-static-mechanic-DRAFT.md:3` — and **F-1363-1 (s1363) already found the one surface that had lost the qualifier and cured it in `f1308ee9` with an explicit DO-NOT-AUTHOR.** Post-launch is unsatisfied today (`git tag` carries no version tag). **(2) `W1-02`, `W1-06` (2): SHIPPED.** `reviews/w1-02-living-water.md` and `reviews/w1-06-vista.md` exist and `vista` is live in **6 `src/` files**; their ladder rows were retired per §4. **(3) `PB-02` (1): SHIPPED at `5a153e95`** — *“✅ PB-01+02 … EVENT PARITY PROVEN”* (`BACKLOG:1358`). **(4) `MP-05`/`MU-01`/`SS-04`/`ED-06`/`ED-07` (5): owner-gated or not-yet-ratified by construction** — MP-05 is *“owner + son, two devices”*, an acceptance **playtest** (co-op is a PARKED named milestone, `BACKLOG:1408`); MU-01 ends *“→ owner picks”*; SS-04 is a DRAFT rung explicitly sequenced *“With/after the Baron task”*; ED-06/07 sit in a **SEED** spec carrying the owner’s own unanswered question (*“Is it overkill? Should we use something existing?”*), ED-07 marked **OWNER-ONLY v1**. ➡️ **THE STRUCTURAL ANSWER, THIRD ROAD TO THE SAME PLACE: THE LEDGER INDEXES WORK BY THREAD AND RUNG NAME, NOT BY EVERY ID TOKEN A SPEC MINTS.** The e10 Static thread is in BACKLOG **48 times** — as *“e10-static-boss”*, *“roster-wiring-e6-e10”*, *“THE STATIC”* — and **never once as `ST-04`**. A set-difference on slice IDs measures **namespace mismatch**, precisely as F-1371-1 found for F-ids. ⚠️ **TWO INSTRUMENT DEFECTS OF MY OWN, BOTH CAUGHT BEFORE THE COUNT REACHED THE HANDOFF.** **(1) COMPOUND RUNG NOTATION IS INVISIBLE TO A PER-ID WORD-BOUNDARY TEST.** BACKLOG ships PB-02 as **`PB-01+02`**, which `\bPB-02\b` cannot match — I read it as unindexed when it is *shipped and gated*. Swept the class: exactly **2 members** repo-wide (`PB-01+02`, `TP-01+02`). **(2) MY `isDecl` HEURISTIC COUNTED A MENTION AS A DECLARATION** — `W1-02` was harvested from a bullet in `e5-deepwater-bundle.md` describing *“the W1-02 water shader, grown up”*. 🚫 **RECOMMENDATION: NOTHING TO BUILD — AND DO NOT BUILD A specs-vs-BACKLOG SLICE-ID GUARD.** Three independent reasons, the third of which is new and is the real contribution: **(a)** it would red **16 rows** against a ledger measured clean; **(b)** its denominator must encode a **seven-way document-class distinction that exists nowhere in the filesystem** — status is a line, never a filename, by house convention; **(c) ⭐ ABSENCE FROM THE LEDGER IS BIDIRECTIONAL.** §4 requires finished rungs to be **retired** from the ladder, so *“absent from BACKLOG”* is equally the signature of **never-started** work and of **completed-and-retired** work — **3 of my 16 (19%) were the latter.** A guard firing on absence cannot tell the two apart, so **it would report finished work as missing** — the false-NOT-DONE shape F-1368-1 named, mechanised and put on a 5-minute cadence. 💡 **THE THROUGH-LINE, AND IT CLOSES THE SET RATHER THAN EXTENDING IT.** s1369: your freshly-built instrument is the most dangerous artifact on a dry board. s1370: the instrument can be right and the inference wrong. s1371: the result can be fabricated because the probe never ran. **s1372: THE INSTRUMENT, THE INFERENCE AND THE PROBE CAN ALL BE SOUND — AND THE *QUESTION* STILL WRONG, BECAUSE IT ASSUMED A KEY THE LEDGER DOES NOT USE.** Both surfaces s1370 offered have now been swept and both dissolved the same way, which is itself the finding: **this factory’s ledger is organised by THREAD, and every audit that joins on a minted ID — F-ids, slice IDs — will keep rediscovering that fact at the cost of a fire.** ➡️ **The rule I’d hand forward: before measuring what an index is missing, verify that the thing you are joining on is the index’s KEY. Ask what the ledger is organised BY, not what tokens appear in it.** ⓘ And the honest footnote: the ST-00..ST-07 block looked like the best finding available to this fire — 8 slices, owner-ratified *yesterday*, in no ledger — and it took one `grep` of the defence to dissolve it. **s1370’s rule (“ask what would make this innocent, and go read THAT”) is what turned a dramatic false finding into a paragraph.**
2925:🟠 **F-1315-2 (s1315, RE-DERIVED — F-1314-1 IS FILED AS A NEW OWNER FORK, BUT ITS FORK WAS ANSWERED BY THE OWNER ON 2026-07-26 AND BANKED; ONE SLIVER OF IT IS GENUINELY NEW).** s1314 put **F-1314-1** on the owner's desk as a NEW item with options *(a) implement stake loss · (b) stop advertising it · (c) rename the field to pure geography*. ✗ **Those are, in order, options (A), (—) and (C) of `tasks/DRAFT-e1-hold-the-claim.md`**, a draft dated 2026-07-26 and re-verified 2026-07-27 whose header reads **⏸️ OWNER-BANKED POST-RELEASE — DO NOT QUEUE**, and which had already traced the same inert flag through the same gameplay consumers (hero spawn, MP spawn centre, world-info label, prop scale) and reached the same conclusion: *nothing can lose because of it.* ✓ **The owner has already ruled, verbatim (`tasks/BACKLOG.md:1735`, re-verified at source this fire — the draft's own pointer to `:1063` has ROTTED):** *"hold-the-claim (stake loss conditions) BANKED post-release (recommendation: E1 strangers lose by body-death; real siege-loss ships with E2 depth — one word reverses)."* ➡️ **So the desk should carry ONE item, not two, and it is not awaiting a first ruling — it is banked with a stated direction.** ✓ **What IS new, and is the part worth keeping:** every consumer the draft traced was a *gameplay* consumer. **`MechanicsManifest.ts:96-99` publishing `posting.lossStakes`, `:108` printing "loss stakes", and `View.ts:192` folding it into the agent's stable prefix are an AGENT-FACING surface that did not exist when the fork was banked.** Under the banked ruling — E1 loses by body-death — advertising a loss stake to an agent is not an open question at all: it contradicts a decided position. **That makes s1314's rec (b) not a fork but the banked ruling applied to a newer surface**, which is a materially cheaper thing to ask for and may not need the owner at all. ⓘ I did **not** act on it: the disposition of a banked fork is attended/owner triage, and my one authored master went to the AP-07 pin-lift. 💡 *Reusable shape: **before filing a fork, grep `tasks/DRAFT-*.md` for its subject.** A banked draft is invisible to every queue sweep by design — it is marked DO-NOT-QUEUE precisely so nothing picks it up — and that same marking is what lets a later fire rediscover its contents and re-ask a question the owner already answered.*
2971:🔬 **F-1274-3 (s1274, MEASURED AT THE RAW + CURED — CONFIRMS F-1269-2, AND NARROWS s1273'S READING OF IT) — THE LANE ARM'S "77.61% IDLE" WAS A READING OF AN IDLE MACHINE TAKEN AFTER THE WORK FINISHED, AND IT WAS PRINTED AS "idle during 8-child arm".** `logs/session-scratch/s1268/child-scaling-v2.mjs:53-59` schedules its one CPU observation with a hard-coded `setTimeout(…, 3500)`. Two measured facts make that a claim rather than a measurement: **(1)** `top -l 2` is not instantaneous — three consecutive runs on this machine took **1815 / 1786 / 1780 ms**, and the block v2 parses is the **SECOND** sample, so the kept reading corresponds to ~3500+~1000 ms in and the command does not return until **~5290 ms** in; **(2)** the two arms differ ~2.4× in length — the fire arm's 8-child reps ran **10.14 / 10.50 / 9.92 s** (3500 ms = ~36% in, a genuine mid-arm reading that captured all eight children at ~54.5% CPU each), while the **lane** arm's ran **4.06 / 4.18 / 4.33 s**. 🔑 **PROVEN AT THE RAW CAPTURE, NOT INFERRED FROM THE EMPTY ARRAY** — the alternative explanation (an nvm-node naming difference defeating the `\bnode\b` filter) is refuted by `topRaw` in `child-scaling-lane.json`: it reads **"3 running"** and contains **no node process anywhere in a list sorted BY CPU** (top entry `com.apple.Virtua` at **20.7%**). Eight saturated children cannot be absent from a CPU-sorted list. **The children had already exited: a timing failure, not a filter failure.** ⚠️ **SCOPE — THIS NARROWS s1273's §E2, WHICH SAID LEAVING IT BROKEN "POISONS AN OWNER-GATED DECISION".** It does not. F-1270-4 states its confirming test in **throughput multipliers** (*"~7–12× confirms the mechanism, ~3× refutes it"*), and those come from `runN()`'s hrtime around child exit — **a separate and sound path**. Only the *corroborating* idle/child-CPU field was invalid, and only on the short arm. **v2's CONCLUSION stands; one of its supporting fields did not.** The fix still matters because the owner will RUN this instrument, and it would print a false label at the moment of confirmation. 🔒 **CURE: `logs/session-scratch/s1274/child-scaling-v3.mjs`** (new file — **v2 and both its result JSONs left byte-untouched per the Retention Law**). The throughput half is deliberately **unchanged**, including the workload constant, so the numbers stay comparable with the v2 runs. What changed: the delay is **derived from the median 8-child time this machine just measured** (`fraction 0.5`, compensated for top's own second-sample latency) instead of a constant; the run records `topInvokedAtMs` / `topReturnedAtMs` / `topLatencyMs` / `childrenAliveAtTopInvoke` / `childrenAliveAtTopReturn` so the label is **falsifiable by the reader**; and **the label is earned or withheld** — a reading with zero child rows is marked `INVALID … Do NOT read idlePercent as arm load` and never called "during". An arm too short to contain a valid sample is **skipped and said so** — *an unsampled arm reports nothing, not idle*. 🧪 **BOTH DIRECTIONS EXERCISED:** **fire arm, real run** → `IN-ARM: 8 child row(s) observed, 8/8 still alive when top returned`, idle 44.12%, children ~63.4% each (v2's blind luck on the long arm is now v3's guarantee) · **short-arm mutant** (a copy with the workload cut 9e8→3e7, v3 itself untouched) → 8-child arm **0.18 s** → `observation: SKIPPED — arm ~0.18s is too short … NO SAMPLE TAKEN`, where v2 would have slept 3500 ms and printed an idle number. ⓘ **Stated honestly: the third branch (children die *while* top runs → `INVALID`) is a defensive backstop and was NOT exercised** — with the 0.5 fraction and the 300 ms floor the schedule avoids that regime by construction, so it only fires if load shifts between the reps and the observation.
