4` (main) is **non-monotonic**, so bisect's precondition is violated outright. The discriminating control — **the same commit `a1ec923b8`, same shell, back-to-back** — returned `calls 72 / triangles 146026` and then `calls 73 / triangles 146028`. ➡️ **The ±1 `calls` / ±2 `triangles` component is NOISE, not drift, and no commit can be blamed for it.** ⚖️ **What survives as possibly real:** `geometries 80→81` held steady at 80 across both runs at `a1ec923b8` and reads 81 on main, as does the large `+1682` triangle step — those are **unattributed and NOT bisectable by this predicate**; attributing them needs a denoised statistic (n runs per commit, compare distributions) rather than a byte comparison. 💡 **THE REUSABLE LESSON, which is bigger than this artifact: a number committed as "retained evidence" implies a reproducibility it was never measured to have.** Every reader since 07-25 — including this fire's own first draft, and s1475's standing order to confirm the baselines "byte-unchanged" — treated byte-equality as the pass condition for a quantity that is not byte-stable. A fire obeying that order literally would have blocked a clean slice on someone else's noise. **GATE: closes when either (a) the counts are re-characterised with a measured noise band and the artifact records a tolerance instead of a byte, or (b) the spec stops writing them into the tracked tree.** Until then the churn is the **F-1407-1 artifact-churn class** — any lane or fire running this spec is left with 12 dirty tracked files, which can trip a pre-flight's clean-vs-main test. **Do NOT "refresh" these baselines as a drive-by: it would bless one sample of a noisy quantity as truth and restart the same misreading.** 📐 **MEASURED s1477 — THE DENOISED STATISTIC THE GATE ASKED FOR NOW EXISTS, AND IT CORRECTS THIS ROW ON ONE POINT OF RECORD.** `artifacts/s1477-noise/REPORT.md` (`1b64d48b1`): **crawler n=12, railcar n=10, one commit `659f4efe0`, instrument pinned, `--workers=1`, same shell** — subject fixed, so any spread IS the band. **(1)** Most metrics are already byte-stable: **18 of 20** (crawler), **10 of 18** (railcar). **(2)** `geometries`/`textures` jitter is **COMMON-MODE — every phase-to-phase delta is EXACT** (all 6 railcar phase pairs, single value across all 10 runs: `geometries` 8, 5, 5, −3, −3, 0). The absolutes move; the differences do not, which is why the railcar spec’s live `geometries - baseline.geometries < 8` assertion is sound and has never flaked. **(3)** `calls`/`triangles` jitter **independently per phase**, with a `+1 call ⟺ +2 triangles` signature in **every** sample of **both** specs — the fingerprint of a single 2-triangle quad present or absent in the sampled frame, i.e. a sampling race rather than a rendering change. ⚠️ **THE CORRECTION: this row recorded `geometries 80→81` as "stable across both runs… unattributed and NOT bisectable". At n=12 `coldBaseline.geometries` is HARD-STABLE at 81 (12/12), so it was never the noisy component — it is a reproducible property of the commit and IS attributable.** ⚠️ **AND THE TRAP THE MEASUREMENT EXPOSED: a metric cannot be classified by its NAME.** The same `geometries` is hard-stable in the crawler’s `coldBaseline` and noisy in **four** railcar phases — noise is a property of the **(spec, phase, metric) triple, measured**, so any global whitelist is wrong on this evidence. ✓ **VERIFIED s1477 and load-bearing for the choice of cure: NOTHING READS THESE FILES** — `git grep renderer-count` over all tracked files returns the two specs that WRITE them and otherwise only prose (reviews, BACKLOG, STATUS, masters). No consumer, no guard, no assertion against the committed JSON. ➡️ **CURE QUEUED s1477 as gate disjunct (a), not (b): `tasks/lane-f1476-1-renderer-count-tolerance.md` → lane-a**, goal leaf `f1476-1-renderer-count-tolerance`. **(a) beats (b) because the deltas are exact and carry the regression signal, so "stop writing them" would discard real evidence to fix churn** — the task records