en, and the pinned E2 Baron test UNMOVED. **Node 26.4.0 on every arm**, stated explicitly per F-1527-3. Merge classification: both files **LANE-TOUCHED only**, `git log 3985f42fe..main` over them **EMPTY**, blobs identical across main's working tree, `lane/a` and the gate merge (`34ebe4cd`, `6dfa976a`) — the tree that landed is the tree that was gated. Driver archived `logs/runs-archive/s1528-gate-driver-noop-arms.mjs`. 🚫 No browser boot probe, **reason recorded rather than omitted**: two Node files, a CLI never bundled plus its test, zero `src/`/`e2e/`/config, so a probe would measure main and not this slice. 🔺 **Two non-blocking findings. F-1528-4: the sentinel is SILENT**, while every other terminating path in `readOrders` writes to stderr — a rider sending a slightly-wrong line cannot tell *"my turn was passed"* from *"my orders were consumed"* **at the moment it happens** (`calls` and the event log distinguish them only afterwards). A one-line stderr note would make the free turn observable, which is exactly the property F-1527-1 found missing in the neighbouring cure; fold it into whichever master next opens this file. **F-1528-5: nothing yet caps a rider that never sends either sentinel.** F-ER02-2 and **F-ER02-1** are two halves of one billing defect — this merge supplies the *ability* to hold; it does not stop the surprise storm minting turns nobody asked for. **F-ER02-1 is the next fire-authorable ER-02 repair and its surface `scripts/gr-sim.mjs` is FREE as of this merge.** 📣 GZ-01 skipped deliberately (factory instrumentation, no player surface).
5446:- 🔧 **F-ER02-1 CORRECTIVE AUTHORED + DISPATCHED s1528 → `lane-b-f1528-1-order-failure-surprise-coalesce.md` (lane-b, FIRE-AUTHORED), leaf registered `queued` in the same commit.** 🏁 **THIS IS THE LAST OF THE THREE FIRE-AUTHORABLE ER-02 PROTOCOL REPAIRS — F-ER02-2 and F-ER02-3 both SHIPPED today (`b55e6ac5`, `c65e6b6d`), and this fire's own two drains freed `src/agent/` and `scripts/gr-sim.mjs` at once.** ⭐ **THE LOAD-BEARING AUTHORING DECISION: THE CURE WAS *DERIVED*, NOT PICKED OFF THE REVIEW'S MENU — and that is what makes it fire-authorable at all.** §5 recommendation 2 names **three** options (*retire an order after N identical failures* · *coalesce `order_failure` surprises* · *let `advanceToTurn` rate-limit surprise-minted turns*), and choosing among three prescribed alternatives is normally an attended/owner call a fire may not make. 🔎 **Re-reading `src/agent/StandingOrders.ts` on main showed the second is not really an option at all — it is the file finishing a rule it already applies one line above.** `private status(...)` opens with `if (record.status === status && record.reason === reason) return;`, so an unchanged status appends **no** `order_status` event: *the file has already decided that "the same thing, again, is not news."* But `private fail(...)` calls `status(...)` and then calls `surprise('order_failure', …)` **unconditionally** — **so the surprise escapes the very de-dupe its own sibling line applies.** That asymmetry IS the defect, and restoring an invariant the file already asserts is authorable where the other two are not: **option 1 changes what an ORDER means to a rider, and option 3 fixes only the headless door while leaving the browser storming.** ✓ **All four links of the mechanism read on main, not inherited** — `fail` raises on every failing tick → `surprise()` sets `needsRider` and advances the sequence → `advanceToTurn` mints a turn on `surpriseSeq > this.lastSurpriseSeq` → `readOrders` blocks until orders are submitted, re-arming the same failing order. **Break link 1 and the loop cannot close; nothing else in the chain needs to change.** 📊 The measurement being cured, from §3.1 (`e2-trestle` seed 01, trail): no orders **15** submissions / wave 14 · the metered card **34** / wave 14 · 3 palisade decoys **341** / wave 14 (**374 %** of the doctrine's whole 100k budget) · **one dark seam** (`gold-seam-4`, published `active:false` in the very first VIEW) **1,200 capped — still at WAVE 1, ~997 %**, and an uncapped earlier form wrote **3,074 turns / 76 MB**. `outcome.calls` is what AP-07 exports as `num_turns`, so this is the economy axis, not tidiness. 🚫 **SCOPE DELIBERATELY NOT WIDENED — and the held-out half is named rather than forgotten: `claim_damage` is the review's SECOND storm trigger** (it fires on every `building_damaged` event; on `e2-incline` building multiplied protocol cost **7.75×** for **0** extra waves) — but it has **no status/reason pair to de-dupe against**, so curing it needs a rate-limit or a window, i.e. a genuine design choice. The master orders it **REPORTED as still open, not folded in**; mixing the two would make both ungateable. ⓘ The master **pre-declares that a pin MOVE is a plausible, honest outcome** rather than a failure — the cure removes repeated events from the event log — and that a moved pin is a **STOP-and-report with before/after numbers, never a re-pin** (F-1441-3). 🛡️ **Its firewall carries an explicit carve-out written from F-1528-2, filed by this same fire an hour earlier:** `f1526-1`'s firewall forbade editing existing tests while its scope *required* editing a byte-stable snapshot fixture, leaving its runner to choose between violating the firewall and shipping nothing — **here adding a test is expected and editing an existing assertion is a STOP-and-report, not a silent judgement call.** All four citation keys proved to return **1 on main before being written down** (F-1425-2), each on one visible line; the fourth is deliberately the `f1527-1` merge content so a 0 accuses **lane staleness** rather than the file. **GATE: drain when lane-b reports; the before/after `outcome.calls` for an unsatisfiable-order arm STATED WITH ITS RATIO, both pins named individually (`byte-for-byte` and `E2 Baron`) with any move reported rather than re-pinned, the both-directions proof that a SECOND, DIFFERENT failure is still surfaced (a cure that silences it is worse than the storm), `node -v` stated per F-1527-3, and `git diff --name-only` showing exactly `src/agent/StandingOrders.ts` + `scripts/gr-sim.test.mjs`.**
