5586:- 🔺 **[F-1637-2] THE FACTORY'S OWN E2E GATES CALL A HARDCODED **PRODUCTION** ORIGIN, AND STUBBING IT IS PER-SPEC OPT-IN (raised s1637 at the SEA-1 drain; OWNER'S DESK — a harness-wide change, not this slice's business).** The SEA-1 runner stubbed `**/api/telemetry` in `lb-01` and mentioned in one passing clause that *"the live endpoint hit a 429 during console-clean Playwright runs."* **That aside is the finding.** ✅ **VERIFIED BY READING, not by grep-inference:** `src/app/GameApi.ts:1` is `export const GAME_API_ORIGIN = 'https://gold-rush-3in.pages.dev';` — a **hardcoded production origin**, not same-origin and not env-resolved; `gameApiUrl()` at `:3-5` simply concatenates onto it; `src/telemetry/runBeacon.ts:89` calls `await fetch(gameApiUrl('/api/telemetry'), …)`. **Therefore any spec that gets far enough to fire the beacon and does not intercept that route makes a live call to the deployed site from inside a gate.** Of **397** e2e specs, **5** reference `api/telemetry` at all (`lb-01` as of this merge, plus `locked-win`, `release-base-path`, `terrain3d-default`, `tl-01-run-telemetry`) — interception is opt-**in**, so the default is to call production. 💸 **Two costs, and the second is the one that bites us:** the factory writes telemetry into the live site while gating, and **production rate-limiting can manufacture reds that look exactly like ordinary tree reds** — the 429 above is a real instance, and it cost this slice's runner a debugging detour before it guessed the cause. That is the F-1457-1 shape (an instrument's red wearing a tree red's clothes) arriving through a network boundary instead of a wrong server. ⚠️ **HONEST LIMIT — DO NOT CITE A COUNT FROM THIS ROW.** The **mechanism** is proven and **one instance** is proven; the **exposed subset is NOT measured.** Only specs that complete a run fire the beacon, and identifying those needs more than a grep — "392 specs are exposed" would be exactly the over-claim this row exists to avoid. ➡️ **RECOMMENDED CLASS FIX (fix the class, not the instance): a default route stub at the config/fixture level, so specs opt OUT of interception rather than opting in.** ⛔ **NOT taken by this fire, deliberately:** it touches every spec's harness, it is disjoint from SEA-1's business, and a wrong default here silently blinds the four specs that legitimately assert on telemetry. **GATE: owner's word on whether gates may reach the public internet at all (a one-line ruling settles it), then a lane. Nothing else is blocked on this — it is a hygiene ceiling, not a live break.** ⬅️ **SCOPE CORRECTED s2109 (F-2109-1) — READ BEFORE BUILDING THE CURE ABOVE.** Every coordinate in this row is INTACT ~470 fires on (`GameApi.ts:1`, `:3-5`, `runBeacon.ts:89`), and the census drifted only benignly (397 → 425 specs, 5 → 6 referencing `api/telemetry`). **What is too narrow is the scope: this row measures ONE endpoint of FIVE on that origin — `/api/standings` (`Game.ts:7008`), `/api/stats` (`liveStats.ts:4`), `/api/bug-report` (`ComplaintDesk.ts:217`) and `/api/redeem` (`ComplaintDesk.ts:258`) sit behind the same hardcoded `GAME_API_ORIGIN`, and four of the five are POST writes to the live site.** All five predate this row, so nothing grew under it. ➡️ **Therefore the RECOMMENDED default stub must be keyed on the ORIGIN (`https://gold-rush-3in.pages.dev/**`), never on `**/api/telemetry`** — keyed on the route it would look like the class fix while leaving four production write paths open. ⚖️ **And this row's GATE is understated: the one-line owner ruling covers five endpoints and four writes, including a `/api/standings` POST that submits a county-standings score — not a lone telemetry beacon.** ⚠️ The exposed subset remains UNMEASURED for all five (this row's own honest limit, extended): exposure is not uniform — `/api/standings` early-returns on a pinned non-bench seed (`Game.ts:6986-6988`), and the `ComplaintDesk` writes need a spec to drive that UI.

