# Armored Railcar damage reads before defeat

Wave 4 turns `plate-e2-boss-component.png` into a real boss GLB. The approved visual direction is a long, low siege engine: dominant armored boiler, bunker-like cabin, unequal drive wheels, exposed running gear, a deep reinforced cowcatcher/ram, near-black iron, structural brass, and restrained teal agent-tech. A fresh reference-blind review returned **SHIP** after the initial toy-like proportions were replaced.

The production interface is three base-centered mesh nodes with identity transforms and default morph weight `0`:

- `Railcar_Wheels` / `Damage_BentWheels`
- `Railcar_Boiler` / `Damage_VentingBoiler`
- `Railcar_Cabin` / `Damage_CrackedCabin`

The runtime must drive a component's morph while it is still alive, beginning at the existing `<=50% HP` damaged threshold or proportionally across remaining live HP. Waiting for defeat would hide the deformation because defeated components are no longer presented as live boss parts.

Verified asset contract: 10,948 triangles, one embedded 1024-square atlas, three primitives all bound to material `0`, no source or GLB cameras/lights/animations, 2.40 x 1.202 x 1.248279 units, and SHA-256 `2abe1fceb5bf7f8e9ea3ba4c2dc4a42e28aa7d9e04b2327d9842862ae48d99b9`.

The evidence camera keeps the actual 42-degree vertical run-camera pitch and rail dimensions (0.78 gauge, rail top y=0.125); only camera distance is shortened to make the review image legible.

Related: [[Gold Rush MOC]] · [[2026-07-14-Gold-Rush-armored-railcar-wave-4]]

